    "title": "A=1 core-free two-packet bounded-divisor normal form",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "two distinguished row radicals, regular determinant, and contact divisor",
    "statement": "Both core-free residual-degree-two packets have two distinguished row radicals with row tails of degree at most two and Forney tails of degree at most three. The regular determinant is their product times a tail of degree at most one, with the unique ordinary triple incidence consuming the full tail in the second packet. The contact divisor gives a signed Picard relation of degree exactly one.",
